From 2dab8077522c64c633d9071bf3f79f348efddc8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:55:35 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] feat(db): add PostgreSQL schema, ERD and data dictionary
 reverse-engineered from the front-end

The app keeps everything in localStorage (eight resto_pos_*_v1 keys). db/ holds the
relational form of that data for a backend:

- schema.sql: 19 tables, 8 views, calculation functions (discount, service charge, PB1,
  per-batch stock deduction) and a table-status trigger. Every column that comes from a
  TypeScript field is tagged [src: Interface.field] in its COMMENT.
- ERD.md and DATA_DICTIONARY.md: generated from the live schema (Mermaid diagram,
  relations, columns, CHECK rules, indexes) plus findings about code behaviour that
  shaped the design, each with the source line.
- seed.sql: generated from initialData.ts and authRoles.ts.
- tests: 72 scenario checks, 272,190-case parity check of SQL vs posCalculations.ts,
  and a coverage check that every field in src/types/pos.ts has a column or is derived.
  Run everything with: bash db/tests/run.sh

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
